From 270a4e767720041c3c3f29b93a55f2f7742c86c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:09:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/15] Add Phase 0 substrate: client_facts store,
 discoverClient, Jev client
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

client_facts (schema.ts) is a new, additive table — one row per
(engagement, fact key) with source/status/confidence provenance. Nothing
existing writes to or reads from it yet; it's the shared layer future
per-field resolvers will read from instead of each product asking the
same question a different product, a connected account, or the client's
own site already answered.

discoverClient(engagementId) pulls Pin-Down's existing crawl pipeline
(discovery-prefill/voice-scraper/design-scraper — reused, not rewritten)
out to the client level and writes its output into client_facts under the
same field-key names worker-registry.ts's WorkerConfigField already uses,
so a later resolver can look facts up directly. No-ops cleanly when no
domain is on file yet.

jev.ts is a first-draft client for Jev via OpenRouter's beta alpha/
decisions endpoint (typed Choice/Score/Noul questions against a shared
state, not chat completions). Its request/response shape is built from
public docs only and is explicitly flagged as needing verification
against a real API key before any caller relies on it.

None of the three pieces are wired into any existing worker, checker, or
UI yet — that's the next phase.
