From 39429f14af73e47be565e75c3c919482228d5ce1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:15:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/15] Add account-harvest hook for Calendly/HubSpot/Klaviyo
 (Phase 1, slice 1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

harvestAccountMetadata(engagementId, provider, credentialValue) pulls each
provider's own account-identity endpoint after a credential connects and
writes results into client_facts (Phase 0) — Calendly /users/me (timezone;
connecting IS choosing bookingPlatform, no inference needed), HubSpot
/account-info/v3/details (portalId, timezone — the exact field
worker-registry.ts's own comment currently calls "not derivable from
anything on file"), Klaviyo /accounts (org name, timezone, website —
seeds primaryDomain via client-profile.ts's existing setter when the
engagement has none yet).

Wired into the one real trigger point: the Composio OAuth callback, right
after a connection is linked to a specific engagement (a vault-only save
with no engagementId has nowhere to write facts, so it's skipped there).
Fire-and-forget from the route — a harvest failure must never turn a
successful credential connect into a redirect error, and
harvestAccountMetadata itself never throws past a single provider's own
try/catch.

Deliberately scoped to 3 of the 5 Composio-managed providers
(composio-providers.ts's PROVIDER_TOOLKIT_MAP also lists mailchimp and
ghl_calendar) — no verified account-metadata field mapping for either yet,
so they're left for a later slice rather than guessed at. Every response
shape here is built from prior research, not a live call this session
could make; each harvester reads defensively and is flagged in the file
header as needing confirmation against a real connected account.

Not yet built: the generic per-field Jev-scored resolver (jev.ts's
endpoint itself is still unverified against a real key) and the
paste-a-key equivalent of this hook for non-OAuth providers.
