The user supplied TypeSafe's own primary documentation (docs.typesafe.ai)
this turn, which fully confirms the request/response contract this file
previously had to guess at (three defensively-parsed possible shapes).
Replaced entirely:

- Real endpoint: POST https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone, body
  {state, model, questions}, response {model, answers, usage}.
- Real per-type shapes: Choice returns {choice, confidence,
  probabilities}; Score returns {score, confidence, legend,
  probabilities}; Noul returns only {noul} — no separate confidence
  field, confirmed by the docs' own explanation (a two-outcome
  distribution needs no separate spread measure).
- costInCents is now an unrounded float, not integer cents — llm.ts's
  recordRunUsage rounds to whole cents, which this project's own earlier
  review flagged as hiding real cost on anything this cheap; Jev calls
  are cheaper still, so this doesn't repeat that bug.
- Base URL/model id are resolved through one function (JEV_TRANSPORT env
  var), isolating the one thing that's still genuinely unverified —
  OpenRouter's exact hosting of this endpoint, since openrouter.ai is
  blocked by this session's own network egress and couldn't be tested
  directly. TypeSafe's own direct endpoint is the default; switching
  transports is a one-line env change, not a rewrite.

field-resolvers.ts is the generic per-field resolver this was blocked on:
resolveFieldsFromEvidence(engagementId, evidenceFactKey, questions) reads
whatever's already in client_facts (Phase 0/1's website crawl or account
harvest), asks Jev every relevant question about it in one call per
TypeSafe's own "ask multiple questions together" guidance, and writes
each answer back with its confidence. Includes one concrete resolver,
resolveTrafficTemperature: pin-down's traffic_temperature is a real,
closed 3-option enum in schema.ts, a clean Choice candidate. Its sibling
field, offerVertical, is deliberately NOT resolved this way — schema.ts's
own comment confirms vertical is free text with no fixed taxonomy in this
app today, and forcing it into a Choice would mean inventing one, a real
product decision, not something to slip in inside a resolver.

Not yet wired into any trigger, checker, or UI — still Phase 1 substrate,
same as the rest of this phase.
