discoverClient had exactly one caller in the whole codebase (account-
harvest.ts's own fallback when a harvest ran and no domain existed yet)
— a client whose domain gets set through Pin-Down's own live setup flow
never got crawled at all unless they separately connected an OAuth
credential afterward. Fixed at the one real place a domain is set today:
bridges/pin-down/route.ts now kicks off discoverClient (fire-and-forget,
never blocking the response) when marketingDomain is new or changed.

discoverClient itself now chains into resolveTrafficTemperature right
after writing rawVoiceCorpus, so the one Jev resolver built so far
actually fires end-to-end from a real trigger instead of needing a
separate manual call. Wrapped in try/catch: no TYPESAFE_API_KEY/
OPENROUTER_API_KEY configured is the expected state in every environment
today, not a bug to surface as an error.

paste-key-harvest.ts is the paste-a-key equivalent of account-harvest.ts
— the trigger for every provider that isn't Composio/OAuth-managed
(Cal.com, Twilio, Instantly, Apollo, Whop, and the rest), wired into
/api/credentials' real storeCredential call site. Deliberately ships with
zero providers implemented: none has a verified account-metadata endpoint
yet, and guessing at one is exactly the mistake jev.ts's own rewrite this
session corrected. The hook is real and fires on every paste-a-key save;
coverage grows one verified provider at a time, same shape
account-harvest.ts already established.

Found and left alone, not fixed: tests/unit/engagement-bridges-pin-down-
route.test.ts already fails 8/10 on this branch's last commit (9cdedd2),
before any change in this commit — confirmed by reverting these exact
files to that commit and re-running (identical 8 failed/2 passed both
before and after). Pre-existing and unrelated to this work.
