The user pasted Mailchimp's own API Root reference page (mailchimp.com/
developer/marketing/api/root/) directly into this session. harvestMailchimp
is built against that exact schema, not inferred:

- account_name -> operatorName (falls back to contact.company)
- account_timezone -> timezone
- account_industry -> offerVertical, a direct pass-through, not a Jev
  classification — offerVertical is genuinely free text in this app
  (schema.ts's own comment), so Mailchimp's own free-text industry field
  needs no taxonomy invented to use it, unlike trafficTemperature/
  castingChoice which needed Jev because they're closed enums.
- Connecting Mailchimp at all is choosing it as emailPlatform, same
  definitional pattern as the other 3 providers.

One real implementation detail from Mailchimp's own Fundamentals docs
(also pasted this session): the API has no single base URL — it requires
a datacenter prefix (e.g. "us6") that isn't returned by any endpoint, only
present as a suffix already on the API key itself ("...abcde-us6").
harvestMailchimp parses it from the same credential value used for auth
rather than requiring a second stored field.

This is now 4 of 5 Composio-managed providers covered (only ghl_calendar
remains, still blocked on a verified endpoint). Verified: typecheck
clean, pre-existing test failure count unchanged (8/10 in
engagement-bridges-pin-down-route.test.ts, same as every prior commit).
