Discovered this session that this sandbox's network egress blocks vendor
doc *websites* but not plain git clones of public GitHub repos — a real,
useful distinction, not the blanket block assumed earlier. Used it two
ways:

1. Cloned GoHighLevel's OFFICIAL OpenAPI spec repo
   (github.com/GoHighLevel/highlevel-api-docs) and checked the already-
   shipped harvestGHLLocation against it directly. Every field name
   (name, website, timezone, email, phone, business.*, social.*) and the
   `location` root-wrapper match exactly — and it independently confirms
   this session's own correction of the relayed "v3" header: the spec's
   own required-header enum is literally ["2021-07-28"], only. No changes
   needed; this is a verification commit for that harvester's confidence
   tier, not a fix.

2. Cloned Twilio's OFFICIAL spec repo (github.com/twilio/twilio-oai) and
   built harvestTwilioA2PStatus from it — GET /v1/Services/{sid}/
   Compliance/Usa2p (messaging.twilio.com), Basic auth
   (accountSid:authToken), campaign_status field. This is the first
   Twilio-sourced fact this app derives, closing a gap named early in
   this session's own research (smsA2p10dlcStatus).

Handled honestly, not force-mapped: Twilio's raw campaign_status has no
1:1 mapping onto this app's own 3-state sms_a2p_10dlc_status enum
(not_started/brand_registered/campaign_approved) — that enum spans both
brand registration and campaign approval, and this one endpoint only
covers the campaign half. Only writes the two states resolvable without
also calling Twilio's separate BrandRegistrations resource: VERIFIED ->
campaign_approved (Twilio's own semantics, exactly what
sendSmsForTenant's compliance gate checks for), any other campaign status
-> brand_registered (not a guess — Twilio requires an approved brand
before a campaign can exist at all, so a campaign's mere existence
implies that step passed). No campaign in the list at all is genuinely
ambiguous between the other two states from this one endpoint and writes
nothing, rather than guessing.

Also checked Whop's spec (github.com/distilled-mirror/spec-mirror-whop,
an unofficial mirror carrying its own "not an accurate representation of
actual API behavior" disclaimer) and found its `servers` field disagrees
with this app's own already-working probe.ts/client.ts on the base path
(api.whop.com/api/v1 vs. this app's api.whop.com/v1). Not changed —
trusting this app's live, tested code over an admittedly-unofficial
mirror; flagged, not silently resolved either way.

Verified: typecheck clean, zero new lint issues, pre-existing test
failure count unchanged.
