From 64bb76eb671d690a4d604117159145565a1792d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 01:48:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] Phase 2, items 8-9: enable-time field check, narrow not
 full-dossier
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Library's Enable route (workers/[workerId]/enable) previously checked
only that the whole PRODUCT had been onboarded (a presence check) —
never this specific worker's own secret or blocking fields. A worker
could be flipped on with a missing credential or a genuinely-irreducible
blocking field and only find out at its next scheduled run, via
skill.ts's own separate gate.

Now calls getMissingRequiredFields before installing/enabling — the same
function Phase 2's first piece (field-writeback.ts) already taught to
resolve everything it can before reporting anything missing, so this
reports exactly what's still missing after every available credential/
crawl/Jev signal had its chance, never a blanket "go configure this."
That's items 8 and 9 together, through one mechanism: the enable-time
credential-only prompt (8) and the narrow non-dossier ask for genuinely
irreducible fields (9) are the same list, since getMissingRequiredFields
already returns exactly what a checker still can't fill in, whether
that's a secret or a real business fact — no separate "secrets-only"
check needed on top of it.

Deliberately no bridgeHref on this new 422 shape — that field is what
triggers the existing ProductOnboardingGateModal, which is about running
the whole PRODUCT's onboarding worker, a different problem from this
worker's own missing fields. Checked the frontend caller
(workers-panel.tsx) before wiring anything: it only acts on a 422 when
